d 'GEPWREG': module for percentile weights regression: the effect of the covariates at a quantile of the outcome
d
d  gepwreg estimates the effect of the covariates on an outcome for
d the units located at a target quantile of the outcome, at the
d initial quantile (the outcome before the contribution of chosen
d covariates), or along the rank of an observed covariate, with the
d percentile weights of Araar (2016): Gaussian kernel weights on
d the percentile scale. The effect at a quantile of the outcome is
d estimated in two steps: unit-level effects from a heterogeneity
d model fitted on the whole sample (a conditional quantile
d regression, or interactions with observed variables) are averaged
d with the percentile weights on the rank of the outcome, and the
d estimator converges to the unconditional quantile partial effect.
d Standard errors come from the influence function of the whole
d procedure, with Taylor linearisation under a complex survey
d design declared by svyset, or from a bootstrap that re-runs the
d whole procedure; the bandwidth is the MSE-optimal plug-in. ref()
d gives the effect for a given household, which holds the
d composition of the group at the quantile fixed, and graph() draws
d the profile of the effects across percentiles with a simultaneous
d confidence band and a test that the effect is constant across
d percentiles. merr corrects the interaction model for classical
d measurement error in the heterogeneity variables. gepwreg_setable
d compares the standard errors; a dialog box is included, and the
d examples of the help run from clickable links (gepwreg_examples).
d The paper that documents the estimators is included as an
d ancillary file (gepwreg_paper.pdf). 
d
d KW:  percentile weights regression
d KW: unconditional quantile partial effect
d KW: quantile regression
d KW: heterogeneous effects
d KW: survey design
d KW: influence function
d KW: bandwidth selection
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261005
d
d Author: Abdelkrim Araar,  Universite Laval 
d Support: email aabd@@ecn.ulaval.ca
d
f gepwreg.ado
f gepwreg.dlg
f gepwreg.sthlp
f gepwreg_examples.ado
f gepwreg_paper.pdf
f gepwreg_setable.ado
f ../b/bkf98I.dta
